   "cNativeScalarMBps": 471,
   "portableSHA256InTheGameMBps": "≈379 (2.0 s for 757.7 MB)"
  },
  "note": "no cheaper block function: the Swift code already beats this C in wasm (its first pass runs in V8's baseline tier, still below even when corrected); a single-stream -msimd128 build would gain little"
 },
 "levers": [
  "Host only: prefetch from the page (same HTTP cache) in the program's read order while the program starts at once, so downloads overlap the ~2.6 s of SHA and LZ4 — a first visit then approaches max(download, startup) instead of their sum (12.8 s at 100 Mbit/s in W3b)",
  "Core/Runtime: on WASI the loading packages are computed at creation (OriginalConcurrentInputs: inline where the native hosts use a thread behind the menu), so ~728 MB are read and digested before the menu's first frame though the menu needs the 29.7 MB startup package; computing them at first use (or in bounded slices during the menu's sleeps) with the same order and errors would bring the first frame to ~1 s; needs the existing hosts' gate",
  "A SIMD128 SHA-256 digesting four entries at once (~2× scalar), the digests and their manifest order unchanged — medium",
  "wasi-threads (parallel digests, loads) — large"
 ],
