 "existingHosts": "No Core, Runtime, Package.swift or Swift change",
 "review": "Independent, read-only: the code OK with low items queued (profile start should pause the new worker until Profiler.start and set the sampling interval; a lost profile without --metrics or after a reload; served counted before the read; the metrics file lost if its body fails to parse; usage text). The attribution holds (corrected: 757.7 MB digested, ~379 MB/s; wasm-to-js is all WASI imports), but the first conclusion — threads as the only lever — missed two cheaper behaviour-identical levers: the prefetch overlapping the startup from the page, and computing WASI's loading packages at first use instead of at creation (first frame ~1 s); and a SIMD multi-buffer SHA. Recorded as the next tasks.",
 "boundaries": [
  "Profiles start when the worker attaches (its first milliseconds may be missed)",
  "WebKit not profiled (no DevTools protocol on its build)"
 ]
}